@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bmfire-nouns`
IMPORT `bmfire-claim`

-- TEST SCAFFOLDING, not rules. Generated by scratchpad/vn20/genfix.py from the nouns, so
-- every enumeration below mirrors a record exactly. The rule modules require every fact
-- as an input; these helpers let a test name only the facts that are TRUE (or, for the
-- Insured's conduct, only the lapses), and set every other one to its ordinary value.
-- Defaults here are the tests' convention, never the Rules'.

§ `Test fixtures`

§§ `The facts of an incident`

DECLARE `A fact in a test` IS ONE OF
    `fact — an actual flame`
    `fact — the flame was out of control`
    `fact — the flame burned in abnormal conditions`
    `fact — the flame was a fire source meant for everyday living`
    `fact — violence or force was used or threatened`
    `fact — for a political, religious, ideological or similar purpose`
    `fact — by persons acting on behalf of or in connection with an organisation`
    `fact — an earthquake or volcanic eruption`
    `fact — another convulsion of nature`
    `fact — an underground fire`
    `fact — a forest, bush, grassland, wilderness or jungle fire, or the burning of land to clear it`
    `fact — a direct lightning strike`
    `fact — the lightning changed the shape of the property or set it alight`
    `fact — an explosion`
    `fact — the explosion was of a boiler or of gas`
    `fact — the boiler or gas was used for domestic purposes`
    `fact — at a place whose function includes producing gas`
    `fact — an aircraft or other aerial device, or something from one, fell on the property`
    `fact — an act of a person taking part with others in disturbing public order`
    `fact — action of a lawful authority suppressing or limiting such a disturbance`
    `fact — a wilful act of a striker or locked-out worker, to further a strike or resist a lockout`
    `fact — action of a lawful authority preventing or limiting the consequences of such acts`
    `fact — a civil commotion that is part of, or grows into, a popular uprising`
    `fact — a malicious act of any person`
    `fact — the malicious act was a wilful act of strikers, demonstrators or locked-out workers, to further a strike or resist a lockout`
    `fact — malicious erasure, loss, distortion or corruption of information on a computer system or in software, programs or stored data`
    `fact — the damage occurred while the Insured was permanently dispossessed by confiscation or requisition`
    `fact — the damage occurred while the Insured was permanently dispossessed of a building by unlawful occupation`
    `fact — a flood of sea water resulting from an earthquake or volcanic eruption`
    `fact — a storm or tempest`
    `fact — a flood`
    `fact — water overflowing from a natural or artificial water source, reservoir, canal, dam, or water apparatus or pipe`
    `fact — a flood from the sea`
    `fact — frost, subsidence or landslip`
    `fact — water overflowing from a water tank, water apparatus or water pipe`
    `fact — leakage or discharge from an automatic sprinkler installation`
    `fact — impact by a vehicle`
    `fact — impact by an animal`
    `fact — the vehicle or animal was owned or controlled by the Insured, the occupier of the insured premises, or their employees`
    `fact — a riot or rebellion, the event III.1(a)(i) and III.1(a)(iii) both name`
    `fact — a civil commotion`
    `fact — a strike or lockout`
    `fact — war, invasion, act of a foreign enemy, hostilities or warlike operations, or civil war`
    `fact — a violent disturbance, the further event III.1(a)(iii) names`
    `fact — mutiny, popular rising, insurrection, revolution, coup, martial law, or events leading to martial law or curfew`
    `fact — nuclear weapons material`
    `fact — ionising radiation or radioactive contamination from nuclear fuel or nuclear waste`
    `fact — pollution or contamination`
    `fact — the pollution or contamination itself resulted from an insured risk`
    `fact — an insured risk itself resulted from the pollution or contamination`
    `fact — the damage was done by a deliberate act or by sabotage`
    `fact — a computer or chip's handling of a date change, including year 2000 or a leap year, contributed`
    `fact — a change or modification relating to a date change contributed`

GIVEN fs IS A LIST OF `A fact in a test`
GIVETH A `The facts of the incident`
`the facts` fs MEANS
    `The facts of the incident` WITH
        `an actual flame` IS elem `fact — an actual flame` fs
        `the flame was out of control` IS elem `fact — the flame was out of control` fs
        `the flame burned in abnormal conditions` IS elem `fact — the flame burned in abnormal conditions` fs
        `the flame was a fire source meant for everyday living` IS elem `fact — the flame was a fire source meant for everyday living` fs
        `violence or force was used or threatened` IS elem `fact — violence or force was used or threatened` fs
        `for a political, religious, ideological or similar purpose` IS elem `fact — for a political, religious, ideological or similar purpose` fs
        `by persons acting on behalf of or in connection with an organisation` IS elem `fact — by persons acting on behalf of or in connection with an organisation` fs
        `an earthquake or volcanic eruption` IS elem `fact — an earthquake or volcanic eruption` fs
        `another convulsion of nature` IS elem `fact — another convulsion of nature` fs
        `an underground fire` IS elem `fact — an underground fire` fs
        `a forest, bush, grassland, wilderness or jungle fire, or the burning of land to clear it` IS elem `fact — a forest, bush, grassland, wilderness or jungle fire, or the burning of land to clear it` fs
        `a direct lightning strike` IS elem `fact — a direct lightning strike` fs
        `the lightning changed the shape of the property or set it alight` IS elem `fact — the lightning changed the shape of the property or set it alight` fs
        `an explosion` IS elem `fact — an explosion` fs
        `the explosion was of a boiler or of gas` IS elem `fact — the explosion was of a boiler or of gas` fs
        `the boiler or gas was used for domestic purposes` IS elem `fact — the boiler or gas was used for domestic purposes` fs
        `at a place whose function includes producing gas` IS elem `fact — at a place whose function includes producing gas` fs
        `an aircraft or other aerial device, or something from one, fell on the property` IS elem `fact — an aircraft or other aerial device, or something from one, fell on the property` fs
        `an act of a person taking part with others in disturbing public order` IS elem `fact — an act of a person taking part with others in disturbing public order` fs
        `action of a lawful authority suppressing or limiting such a disturbance` IS elem `fact — action of a lawful authority suppressing or limiting such a disturbance` fs
        `a wilful act of a striker or locked-out worker, to further a strike or resist a lockout` IS elem `fact — a wilful act of a striker or locked-out worker, to further a strike or resist a lockout` fs
        `action of a lawful authority preventing or limiting the consequences of such acts` IS elem `fact — action of a lawful authority preventing or limiting the consequences of such acts` fs
        `a civil commotion that is part of, or grows into, a popular uprising` IS elem `fact — a civil commotion that is part of, or grows into, a popular uprising` fs
        `a malicious act of any person` IS elem `fact — a malicious act of any person` fs
        `the malicious act was a wilful act of strikers, demonstrators or locked-out workers, to further a strike or resist a lockout` IS elem `fact — the malicious act was a wilful act of strikers, demonstrators or locked-out workers, to further a strike or resist a lockout` fs
        `malicious erasure, loss, distortion or corruption of information on a computer system or in software, programs or stored data` IS elem `fact — malicious erasure, loss, distortion or corruption of information on a computer system or in software, programs or stored data` fs
        `the damage occurred while the Insured was permanently dispossessed by confiscation or requisition` IS elem `fact — the damage occurred while the Insured was permanently dispossessed by confiscation or requisition` fs
        `the damage occurred while the Insured was permanently dispossessed of a building by unlawful occupation` IS elem `fact — the damage occurred while the Insured was permanently dispossessed of a building by unlawful occupation` fs
        `a flood of sea water resulting from an earthquake or volcanic eruption` IS elem `fact — a flood of sea water resulting from an earthquake or volcanic eruption` fs
        `a storm or tempest` IS elem `fact — a storm or tempest` fs
        `a flood` IS elem `fact — a flood` fs
        `water overflowing from a natural or artificial water source, reservoir, canal, dam, or water apparatus or pipe` IS elem `fact — water overflowing from a natural or artificial water source, reservoir, canal, dam, or water apparatus or pipe` fs
        `a flood from the sea` IS elem `fact — a flood from the sea` fs
        `frost, subsidence or landslip` IS elem `fact — frost, subsidence or landslip` fs
        `water overflowing from a water tank, water apparatus or water pipe` IS elem `fact — water overflowing from a water tank, water apparatus or water pipe` fs
        `leakage or discharge from an automatic sprinkler installation` IS elem `fact — leakage or discharge from an automatic sprinkler installation` fs
        `impact by a vehicle` IS elem `fact — impact by a vehicle` fs
        `impact by an animal` IS elem `fact — impact by an animal` fs
        `the vehicle or animal was owned or controlled by the Insured, the occupier of the insured premises, or their employees` IS elem `fact — the vehicle or animal was owned or controlled by the Insured, the occupier of the insured premises, or their employees` fs
        `a riot or rebellion, the event III.1(a)(i) and III.1(a)(iii) both name` IS elem `fact — a riot or rebellion, the event III.1(a)(i) and III.1(a)(iii) both name` fs
        `a civil commotion` IS elem `fact — a civil commotion` fs
        `a strike or lockout` IS elem `fact — a strike or lockout` fs
        `war, invasion, act of a foreign enemy, hostilities or warlike operations, or civil war` IS elem `fact — war, invasion, act of a foreign enemy, hostilities or warlike operations, or civil war` fs
        `a violent disturbance, the further event III.1(a)(iii) names` IS elem `fact — a violent disturbance, the further event III.1(a)(iii) names` fs
        `mutiny, popular rising, insurrection, revolution, coup, martial law, or events leading to martial law or curfew` IS elem `fact — mutiny, popular rising, insurrection, revolution, coup, martial law, or events leading to martial law or curfew` fs
        `nuclear weapons material` IS elem `fact — nuclear weapons material` fs
        `ionising radiation or radioactive contamination from nuclear fuel or nuclear waste` IS elem `fact — ionising radiation or radioactive contamination from nuclear fuel or nuclear waste` fs
        `pollution or contamination` IS elem `fact — pollution or contamination` fs
        `the pollution or contamination itself resulted from an insured risk` IS elem `fact — the pollution or contamination itself resulted from an insured risk` fs
        `an insured risk itself resulted from the pollution or contamination` IS elem `fact — an insured risk itself resulted from the pollution or contamination` fs
        `the damage was done by a deliberate act or by sabotage` IS elem `fact — the damage was done by a deliberate act or by sabotage` fs
        `a computer or chip's handling of a date change, including year 2000 or a leap year, contributed` IS elem `fact — a computer or chip's handling of a date change, including year 2000 or a leap year, contributed` fs
        `a change or modification relating to a date change contributed` IS elem `fact — a change or modification relating to a date change contributed` fs

§§ `The Insured's conduct`

DECLARE `A lapse in a test` IS ONE OF
    `lapse — misdeclared, misdescribed, gave untrue information, or did not disclose material information about the insured risk`
    `lapse — not: kept the insured property in good repair and took every proper measure to prevent DAMAGE`
    `lapse — not: took steps at once to minimise the loss and recover lost property`
    `lapse — not: notified Bao Minh in writing at once`
    `lapse — not: notified the police at once`
    `lapse — not: supplied at its own expense the information and documents Bao Minh reasonably required, with a sworn statement`
    `lapse — not: supplied the plans and information Bao Minh asked for to repair or replace`
    `lapse — not: did what Bao Minh required to enforce rights against third parties`
    `lapse — the claim was fraudulent`
    `lapse — the Insured, or anyone on its behalf, used fraudulent means to benefit under the policy`
    `lapse — the DAMAGE was caused by a wilful act, or with the connivance, of the Insured`
    `lapse — insured the deductible during the period of the policy`

GIVEN `the day the claim was delivered` IS A DATE
      `the longer period` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      ls IS A LIST OF `A lapse in a test`
GIVETH A `The Insured's conduct`
`conduct with a longer period` `the day the claim was delivered` `the longer period` ls MEANS
    `The Insured's conduct` WITH
        `misdeclared, misdescribed, gave untrue information, or did not disclose material information about the insured risk` IS elem `lapse — misdeclared, misdescribed, gave untrue information, or did not disclose material information about the insured risk` ls
        `kept the insured property in good repair and took every proper measure to prevent DAMAGE` IS NOT elem `lapse — not: kept the insured property in good repair and took every proper measure to prevent DAMAGE` ls
        `took steps at once to minimise the loss and recover lost property` IS NOT elem `lapse — not: took steps at once to minimise the loss and recover lost property` ls
        `notified Bao Minh in writing at once` IS NOT elem `lapse — not: notified Bao Minh in writing at once` ls
        `notified the police at once` IS NOT elem `lapse — not: notified the police at once` ls
        `date the written claim was delivered` IS `the day the claim was delivered`
        `a longer period for the written claim allowed by Bao Minh in writing, in days` IS `the longer period`
        `supplied at its own expense the information and documents Bao Minh reasonably required, with a sworn statement` IS NOT elem `lapse — not: supplied at its own expense the information and documents Bao Minh reasonably required, with a sworn statement` ls
        `supplied the plans and information Bao Minh asked for to repair or replace` IS NOT elem `lapse — not: supplied the plans and information Bao Minh asked for to repair or replace` ls
        `did what Bao Minh required to enforce rights against third parties` IS NOT elem `lapse — not: did what Bao Minh required to enforce rights against third parties` ls
        `the claim was fraudulent` IS elem `lapse — the claim was fraudulent` ls
        `the Insured, or anyone on its behalf, used fraudulent means to benefit under the policy` IS elem `lapse — the Insured, or anyone on its behalf, used fraudulent means to benefit under the policy` ls
        `the DAMAGE was caused by a wilful act, or with the connivance, of the Insured` IS elem `lapse — the DAMAGE was caused by a wilful act, or with the connivance, of the Insured` ls
        `insured the deductible during the period of the policy` IS elem `lapse — insured the deductible during the period of the policy` ls

GIVEN `the day the claim was delivered` IS A DATE
      ls IS A LIST OF `A lapse in a test`
GIVETH A `The Insured's conduct`
`conduct` `the day the claim was delivered` ls MEANS
    `conduct with a longer period` `the day the claim was delivered` NOTHING ls

§§ `Items`

DECLARE `An item feature in a test` IS ONE OF
    `item — not stated in the Policy Summary`
    `item — specifically recorded as insured in this policy`
    `item — an awning, blind, signboard, outside fixture, gate, fence, or movable property in the open`
    `item — a building under construction, renovation or repair`
    `item — every door, window and other opening completed against storm`
    `item — a building left empty or not in use`
    `item — the boiler, economiser, vessel, machine or apparatus under pressure that exploded, or an internal part of it`
    `item — electronic data processing media`
    `item — electrical machinery, apparatus or installation`

GIVEN `the description`  IS A STRING
      `the category`     IS A `A category of property`
      `the sum insured`  IS A NUMBER
      `the actual value` IS A NUMBER
      `already paid`     IS A NUMBER
      fs                 IS A LIST OF `An item feature in a test`
GIVETH AN `An item of insured property`
`an item in full` `the description` `the category` `the sum insured` `the actual value` `already paid` fs MEANS
    `An item of insured property` WITH
        `description` IS `the description`
        `stated in the Policy Summary` IS NOT elem `item — not stated in the Policy Summary` fs
        `category` IS `the category`
        `specifically recorded as insured in this policy` IS elem `item — specifically recorded as insured in this policy` fs
        `an awning, blind, signboard, outside fixture, gate, fence, or movable property in the open` IS elem `item — an awning, blind, signboard, outside fixture, gate, fence, or movable property in the open` fs
        `a building under construction, renovation or repair` IS elem `item — a building under construction, renovation or repair` fs
        `every door, window and other opening completed against storm` IS elem `item — every door, window and other opening completed against storm` fs
        `a building left empty or not in use` IS elem `item — a building left empty or not in use` fs
        `the boiler, economiser, vessel, machine or apparatus under pressure that exploded, or an internal part of it` IS elem `item — the boiler, economiser, vessel, machine or apparatus under pressure that exploded, or an internal part of it` fs
        `electronic data processing media` IS elem `item — electronic data processing media` fs
        `electrical machinery, apparatus or installation` IS elem `item — electrical machinery, apparatus or installation` fs
        `sum insured` IS `the sum insured`
        `actual value at the time of the DAMAGE` IS `the actual value`
        `already paid for earlier losses in this period` IS `already paid`

GIVEN `the description`  IS A STRING
      `the sum insured`  IS A NUMBER
      `the actual value` IS A NUMBER
      fs                 IS A LIST OF `An item feature in a test`
GIVETH AN `An item of insured property`
`an item` `the description` `the sum insured` `the actual value` fs MEANS
    `an item in full` `the description` `property of no category named in III.2(a)` `the sum insured` `the actual value` 0 fs

§§ `Claimed losses`

DECLARE `A loss feature in a test` IS ONE OF
    `loss — destroyed`
    `loss — caused by fire`
    `loss — caused by rain`
    `loss — caused by water other than rain`
    `loss — the rain or water came in through an opening in the structure made by the direct force of the storm`
    `loss — caused by theft, robbery or attempted theft`
    `loss — the item fermented, heated or burned of itself`
    `loss — the item was undergoing a drying process or a process using heat`
    `loss — the item was burned by order of a public authority`
    `loss — the item itself suffered over-running, excessive pressure, short-circuiting, self-heating, arcing or leakage of electricity`
    `loss — insured, or but for this policy would be insured, under a marine policy`
    `loss — the media were repaired, replaced or restored`

-- The figures a loss carries besides its amount: marine recovery, other insurance,
-- reinstatement cost, and the two media costs.
DECLARE `The other figures of a loss` HAS
    `marine recovery`   IS A NUMBER
    `other insurance`   IS A MAYBE `Other insurance on the item`
    `restoring cost`    IS A NUMBER
    `blank media`       IS A NUMBER
    `copying`           IS A NUMBER

`no other figures` MEANS `The other figures of a loss` WITH
    `marine recovery` IS 0
    `other insurance` IS NOTHING
    `restoring cost`  IS 0
    `blank media`     IS 0
    `copying`         IS 0

GIVEN i     IS AN `An item of insured property`
      h     IS A `A head of loss`
      n     IS A NUMBER
      fs    IS A LIST OF `A loss feature in a test`
      o     IS A `The other figures of a loss`
GIVETH A `A claimed loss`
`a loss in full` i h n fs o MEANS
    `A claimed loss` WITH
        `item` IS i
        `head of loss` IS h
        `destroyed` IS elem `loss — destroyed` fs
        `amount of the damage` IS n
        `caused by fire` IS elem `loss — caused by fire` fs
        `caused by rain` IS elem `loss — caused by rain` fs
        `caused by water other than rain` IS elem `loss — caused by water other than rain` fs
        `the rain or water came in through an opening in the structure made by the direct force of the storm` IS elem `loss — the rain or water came in through an opening in the structure made by the direct force of the storm` fs
        `caused by theft, robbery or attempted theft` IS elem `loss — caused by theft, robbery or attempted theft` fs
        `the item fermented, heated or burned of itself` IS elem `loss — the item fermented, heated or burned of itself` fs
        `the item was undergoing a drying process or a process using heat` IS elem `loss — the item was undergoing a drying process or a process using heat` fs
        `the item was burned by order of a public authority` IS elem `loss — the item was burned by order of a public authority` fs
        `the item itself suffered over-running, excessive pressure, short-circuiting, self-heating, arcing or leakage of electricity` IS elem `loss — the item itself suffered over-running, excessive pressure, short-circuiting, self-heating, arcing or leakage of electricity` fs
        `insured, or but for this policy would be insured, under a marine policy` IS elem `loss — insured, or but for this policy would be insured, under a marine policy` fs
        `amount recoverable under the marine policy` IS o's `marine recovery`
        `other insurance` IS o's `other insurance`
        `cost of restoring the item to its condition before the loss` IS o's `restoring cost`
        `cost of blank media` IS o's `blank media`
        `cost of copying the data from back-up or from originals` IS o's `copying`
        `the media were repaired, replaced or restored` IS elem `loss — the media were repaired, replaced or restored` fs

GIVEN i  IS AN `An item of insured property`
      n  IS A NUMBER
      fs IS A LIST OF `A loss feature in a test`
GIVETH A `A claimed loss`
`physical damage to` i `of` n `with` fs MEANS
    `a loss in full` i `physical loss, destruction or damage` n fs `no other figures`

GIVEN `the place` IS A STRING
      ls IS A LIST OF `A claimed loss`
GIVETH A `The loss at one location`
`at the insured location` `the place` ls MEANS
    `The loss at one location` WITH
        `location`                                         IS `the place`
        `an insured location stated in the Policy Summary` IS TRUE
        `claimed losses`                                   IS ls

§§ `Policy Summary, premium, claim`

GIVEN rs   IS A LIST OF `A risk in Section II`
      si   IS A NUMBER
      ds   IS A LIST OF `A deductible stated in the Policy Summary`
      rent IS A BOOLEAN
      rein IS A BOOLEAN
      renw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The Policy Summary`
`a 2026 Summary in full` rs si ds rent rein renw MEANS
    `The Policy Summary` WITH
        `start of the period of insurance`                               IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `end of the period of insurance`                                 IS YMD 2026 12 31
        `risks stated as insured`                                        IS rs
        `total sum insured`                                              IS si
        `deductibles stated`                                             IS ds
        `premium for the period of insurance`                            IS 12000000
        `annual premium`                                                 IS 12000000
        `rent insured under this policy`                                 IS rent
        `Bao Minh agreed to reinstate the sums insured already paid out` IS rein
        `a renewal of an earlier period`                                 IS renw

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF `A risk in Section II`
      si IS A NUMBER
      ds IS A LIST OF `A deductible stated in the Policy Summary`
GIVETH A `The Policy Summary`
`a 2026 Summary` rs si ds MEANS `a 2026 Summary in full` rs si ds FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN r IS A `A risk in Section II`
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A deductible stated in the Policy Summary`
`a deductible for` r `of` n MEANS
    `A deductible stated in the Policy Summary` WITH `risk` IS r, `amount for each loss` IS n

-- A single premium: cover accepted 1 January 2026, paid on the day given.
GIVEN `the day paid` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `The premium`
`a premium paid on` `the day paid` MEANS
    `The premium` WITH
        `date cover was accepted`                  IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `Bao Minh accepted payment in instalments` IS FALSE
        `date the premium was paid in full`        IS `the day paid`
        `instalments`                              IS EMPTY
        `an agreed premium payment term, in days`  IS NOTHING

`the premium paid on 10 January 2026` MEANS `a premium paid on` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 10))

GIVEN s    IS A `The Policy Summary`
      r    IS A `A risk in Section II`
      d    IS A DATE
      f    IS A `The facts of the incident`
      locs IS A LIST OF `The loss at one location`
      p    IS A `The premium`
      es   IS A LIST OF `An endorsement`
      chs  IS A LIST OF `A change under condition VI.3`
      ws   IS A LIST OF `A warranty`
      k    IS A `The Insured's conduct`
      el   IS A BOOLEAN
      paid IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The claim`
`a claim in full` s r d f locs p es chs ws k el paid MEANS
    `The claim` WITH
        `Policy Summary`                                       IS s
        `risk claimed under`                                   IS r
        `date of the DAMAGE`                                   IS d
        `facts`                                                IS f
        `losses`                                               IS locs
        `premium`                                              IS p
        `endorsements relied on`                               IS es
        `changes under condition VI.3`                         IS chs
        `warranties`                                           IS ws
        `conduct`                                              IS k
        `Bao Minh elected to repair or replace`                IS el
        `total already paid for earlier losses in this period` IS paid

-- The ordinary claim: premium paid 10 January 2026, no endorsement, change or
-- warranty, every condition met, written claim delivered ten days after the DAMAGE.
GIVEN s    IS A `The Policy Summary`
      r    IS A `A risk in Section II`
      d    IS A DATE
      f    IS A `The facts of the incident`
      locs IS A LIST OF `The loss at one location`
GIVETH A `The claim`
`a claim` s r d f locs MEANS
    `a claim in full` s r d f locs `the premium paid on 10 January 2026` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY (`conduct` (d PLUS 10) EMPTY) FALSE 0


§§ `The standard case`

-- Policy for 2026, every risk A to J, total sum insured 1,500,000,000 VND, no deductible;
-- the warehouse building, sum insured and actual value 1,000,000,000; DAMAGE on 1 June
-- 2026 at the insured location "Hanoi"; premium paid 10 January; every condition met.

`risk A` MEANS `A. fire, lightning, and explosion of a domestic boiler or gas`
`risk B` MEANS `B. explosion`
`risk C` MEANS `C. aircraft and other aerial devices`
`risk D` MEANS `D. riot, strike and lockout`
`risk E` MEANS `E. malicious damage`
`risk F` MEANS `F. earthquake or volcanic eruption`
`risk G` MEANS `G. storm and tempest`
`risk H` MEANS `H. storm, tempest and flood`
`risk I` MEANS `I. water from tanks, apparatus or pipes`
`risk J` MEANS `J. impact by vehicles or animals`

`every risk` MEANS LIST `risk A`, `risk B`, `risk C`, `risk D`, `risk E`, `risk F`, `risk G`, `risk H`, `risk I`, `risk J`

`the Summary` MEANS `a 2026 Summary` `every risk` 1500000000 EMPTY

`the day` MEANS YMD 2026 6 1

`fire` MEANS LIST `fact — an actual flame`, `fact — the flame was out of control`, `fact — the flame burned in abnormal conditions`

GIVEN ifs IS A LIST OF `An item feature in a test`
GIVETH AN `An item of insured property`
`the building with` ifs MEANS `an item` "the warehouse building" 1000000000 1000000000 ifs

`the building` MEANS `the building with` EMPTY

`the stock` MEANS `an item` "stock of grain" 500000000 500000000 EMPTY

-- A claim with one loss of 200,000,000 to the building.
GIVEN s   IS A `The Policy Summary`
      r   IS A `A risk in Section II`
      fs  IS A LIST OF `A fact in a test`
      lfs IS A LIST OF `A loss feature in a test`
      ifs IS A LIST OF `An item feature in a test`
GIVETH A `The claim`
`a building claim in` s r fs lfs ifs MEANS
    `a claim` s r `the day` (`the facts` fs)
        (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST (`physical damage to` (`the building with` ifs) `of` 200000000 `with` lfs))))

GIVEN r   IS A `A risk in Section II`
      fs  IS A LIST OF `A fact in a test`
      lfs IS A LIST OF `A loss feature in a test`
      ifs IS A LIST OF `An item feature in a test`
GIVETH A `The claim`
`a building claim` r fs lfs ifs MEANS `a building claim in` `the Summary` r fs lfs ifs

-- The standard case with the given losses at the given locations.
GIVEN s    IS A `The Policy Summary`
      r    IS A `A risk in Section II`
      fs   IS A LIST OF `A fact in a test`
      locs IS A LIST OF `The loss at one location`
GIVETH A `The claim`
`a claim at` s r fs locs MEANS `a claim` s r `the day` (`the facts` fs) locs

-- One loss, in an otherwise standard claim.
GIVEN s  IS A `The Policy Summary`
      r  IS A `A risk in Section II`
      fs IS A LIST OF `A fact in a test`
      l  IS A `A claimed loss`
GIVETH A `The claim`
`a claim for the loss` s r fs l MEANS
    `a claim at` s r fs (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST l)))

-- Every reason, claim-level then loss by loss.
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`
`the reasons` c MEANS
    append (`the reasons the whole claim fails` c)
           (concat (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `reasons it is not covered`) (`the assessment of each loss` c)))

